  "full_text": "So, uh, when I lived with my parents, I used to do a show, a five-minute show, where I entertain God, and your ass will follow. Anyway, a lot of those were really good. I didn't see all those. I recorded probably, I don't know, 30 episodes. Anyway, so we just walked down the street. You really got to focus on God. It's like, forget the people. We just got one. Mr. God. Dana told me not to babble so much and say deep stuff. This is embarrassing her. King Terry. Is the crown very heavy, Mr. Guy? No, because he's like, did you suffer? Mr. Guy, Mr. Terry would be like giggling. He'd be like, no, man, I've been through enough fucking torture. No sweat, man. I had my torture, motherfucker. It's going to be cake, huh? Except the crown is not very heavy. Promote peace! Like charcoal to a hot ember and wood to fire, so is a contentious man to kindle strife. A peacemaker is a servant who first is at peace with himself internally, at ease and not agitated, ill-tempered, in turmoil, and therefore not abrasive. Second, he or she works hard to settle quarrels, not start them, is accepting, tolerant, finds no pleasure in being negative. Ever been around Christians who are not peacemakers? Of course. Was it pleasant? Did you sense a servant's heart? Were you built up and encouraged? Was the body of Christ strengthened and supported? You know the answers. Few things are more God-like than peace. When we promote it, pursue it, model it, we are linked directly to Him.",
